From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: read guest code from Wine's read-only alias of a
 view with a noaccess-split host page

Wine keeps a 16 KB host page that holds a committed PAGE_NOACCESS 4 KB page
beside code PROT_NONE (madeira-unix 0279), so the guest's read of the closed
page faults as on x64 Windows. The decoder read the code of such a page, a
byte at a time, through Wine's Mach handler: World of Warcraft's x64 client
took 21.4 M emulated reads in 400 s (run 20261101T191349).

Wine now sends a read-only alias of the view (madeira-unix 0280)
through BTCpu64IosAddAliasMapping with bit 63 of the size set, and the size
equal to the flag alone retires it. IosJitAlias.cpp keeps these in a
query-only table under a sequence count, like the sub-floor windows, and
IosCodeReadAddr gives the alias address of a guest code address. The
decoder's byte source (AdjustAddrForSpecialRegion, as for sub-floor code)
and the disk cache's hashing (GuestCodeBytes) read there; guest addresses,
block identity, executable-range questions and the guest's own accesses are
unchanged. The WOW64 module has no such aliases.

Linear: PLA-516, PLA-514
Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-01-wow-x64-fex.md
Offered-upstream: no; the 16 KB host page is the iOS port's
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/DiskCache.h  |   7 +-
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Frontend.cpp |  18 ++++
 Source/Windows/ARM64EC/IosJitAlias.cpp     | 103 +++++++++++++++++++++
 Source/Windows/WOW64/Module.cpp            |   5 +
 4 files changed, 132 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

